# Clean radio shutdown: no more "wedge until replug" (2026-10-31 02:02)

## the defect
The supervisor stopped children with Process.Kill() = TerminateProcess. For the radio that
means the process dies in the middle of a libusb bulk/control transfer. Observed tonight
four times: the next bring-up either reports "no device 0bda:c820" or blocks inside
libusb (airbridge_radio.exe at 0.03 s CPU for 3-5 minutes, not one devourer log line),
and only a physical replug recovers. Every restart during development cost a replug.

## the fix
radio (src/radio_usb/main.cpp): after listen() it opens the named event
  Local\DropBridgeRadioStop and parks a thread on it; when signalled it closes the
  listener, so accept() fails and the existing clean path runs: StopRxLoop, rx thread
  join, queue stop, device Stop, libusb_release_interface, libusb_close, libusb_exit.
supervisor (src/supervisor/Program.cs): Supervisor.EnsureRadioStopEvent() creates the
  manual-reset event before starting a chain; Child.Stop() signals it for the radio and
  waits up to 4 s before falling back to Kill.

## why an event and not Ctrl+C
The supervisor is a winexe with no console, and the children are created with redirected
stdio, so GenerateConsoleCtrlEvent has no console to attach to. A named event is the
smallest mechanism that works for a winexe parent and a console child.

## verified
both binaries rebuilt clean (supervisor 65 KB, radio 597,504 B) and the offline
supervisor tests (fixed/social env split, invalid mode) still pass.

## not verified yet
The live cycle (start -> graceful stop -> start again without replug) needs a working
dongle; the current one is wedged from before this fix, so it needs one last replug
before the test can run.
